technology, process,

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:51.250
and people, which again, enable
us to respond to these things

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.770
without impacting customers
and without any effort

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:56.260
from customers.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:00.980
So first, to emphasize that
in both of these incidents,

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:04.440
these were mitigated by Google
and Google teams without,

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.790
actually, any impact on
customers, their data,

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:10.500
or on Google or Google's data.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:15.300
And so no data was harmed in
the creation of these events.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:20.170
So at Google, we really think
about security in five pillars,

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:24.350
and we focus product design,
technology, people, and process

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:26.130
around these five pillars.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:28.640
The first of these is really
around Platform Trust,

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:31.240
the core technologies
that really--

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.500
that we create to
drive security,

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.260
protection, monitoring,
identification

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:37.910
within the platform,
and this will

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:41.210
be the focus of most of the
technology piece of this talk.

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:43.580
In addition, we have
technology and products

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.970
focused around the full
lifecycle of data, not just

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:52.250
in data protection-- so
collection, discovery, consent,

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:57.380
access, protection, wipeout,
takeout, that full lifecycle.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:59.270
In addition, we
also have technology

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:02.690
focused around policy and
control and identity and access

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:05.600
