to specify what we think

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.050
is the proper behavior, and
then to detect and enforce

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:11.150
on those behaviors,
as well as for us

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:14.030
to have your identity
be a key thing that

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:17.737
defines what you have access
to and what you authorize on.

00:03:17.737 --> 00:03:19.570
In addition, we have a
fourth pillar focused

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:21.420
around application security.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:23.870
So that's really around
the different pieces that

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:26.390
allow both the
applications we built,

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:28.700
as well as the applications
you build on our platform,

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:32.750
to stay secure, again, from both
visibility, controllability,

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:34.910
protection,
